   includes source, scripts, and binaries. Assets include artwork,
   textures, models, sounds, music, and documentation. Material identified
   as subject to other terms is governed by those terms. This License
   grants only rights the copyright holders have authority to grant.

   Keep the applicable copyright notices and this License with any copy
   or substantial portion of the Work you distribute.

2. Code Permissions
   You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and
   sell the Code, subject to Sections 1 and 4. Any sublicense must
   preserve the obligations of this License for the covered material.

3. Asset Permissions
   You may use and copy Assets as part of the Work. You may distribute
   unmodified Assets as part of an authorized distribution of the Work,
   including a fork or modpack, subject to Sections 1, 4, and 7. Extracting,
   modifying, reusing, or distributing Assets separately requires written
   permission from the applicable copyright holder. Modifying Assets
   within the Work also requires written permission.

   You may depict or adapt Assets in non-commercial community works
   such as screenshots, gameplay videos, reviews, thumbnails, commentary,
   and fan art. Credit the Work where reasonably practicable and make
   clear that your community work is unofficial. This permission does
   not authorize separate distribution of raw Asset files.

4. Anti-Reposting
   You may not publish or mirror an unchanged or substantially unchanged
   copy of the Work as a standalone download on a third-party platform,
   website, or repository without written permission from the applicable
   copyright holder. Changes limited to naming, metadata, or packaging
   do not make a copy substantially different.

   You may publish substantively modified forks or incorporate portions
   of the Code into an independent project under Sections 1 through 3.
   Section 7 permits qualifying modpack distributions.

5. Patent License
   Each contributor grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free
   patent license to make, use, sell, and distribute the Code. This grant
   covers only patent claims the contributor can license that are
   necessarily infringed by their contribution alone or in combination
   with the Code to which they submitted it. The grant is perpetual and
   irrevocable except as stated in this section. If you initiate patent
   litigation alleging that the Work or a contribution to it infringes a
   patent, the patent grants to you under this section for the Work
   terminate upon filing.

6. Contributions
   Material intentionally submitted by an authorized contributor to the
   project maintainer for inclusion in the Work is offered under this
   License unless both parties agree otherwise in writing.

7. Modpacks
   You may distribute an unchanged copy of the Work bundled with other
   mods in a modpack, subject to Section 1 and applicable third-party
   terms. A standalone download remains subject to Section 4. You may
   also link to an authorized download from your modpack. Asset reuse
   remains subject to Section 3.

8. Trademarks and Naming
   You may identify the Work descriptively, for example as the source of
